      "math_academy_id": "e-14854",
      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224890/assets/e5393f15ff154f1f4cc310791790db0fe0ad0d9faa076d10f3f6ec7b481de086.png)",
      "worked_solution": "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-3+2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$",
